    (os/Exit 1)))























(go/type Counter "A Counter is a single named event counter.\nA Counter is safe for use by multiple goroutines simultaneously.\n\nCounters should typically be created using New\nand stored as global variables, like:\n\n\tpackage mypackage\n\tvar errorCount = counter.New(\"mypackage/errors\")\n\n(The initialization of errorCount in this example is handled\nentirely by the compiler and linker; this line executes no code\nat program startup.)\n\nThen code can call Add to increment the counter\neach time the corresponding event is observed.\n\nAlthough it is possible to use New to create\na Counter each time a particular event needs to be recorded,\nthat usage fails to amortize the construction cost over\nmultiple calls to Add, so it is more expensive and not recommended.\n" (struct
    ^{:line 67 :tag string} name
    ^{:line 68 :tag (* file)} file

    ^{:line 70 :tag (atomic/Pointer Counter)} next
    ^{:line 71 :tag counterState} state
    ^{:line 72 :tag counterPtr} ptr))


